From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 20:14:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/16] media: cedrus: vc1: BITS_LEN from slice bit_size,
 raw_coding revert

Use the actual frame bit_size for BITS_LEN instead of the inflated
page-rounded buffer size, preventing VLD from reading uninitialized
memory past the frame end.  Revert raw_coding to ~bitplane_flags
since ffmpeg's slice->raw_coding_flags is always zero for this
stream.

Also remove the CEDRUS_VC1_DEBUG instrumentation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Developed-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>

[Ported to the VC-1 stateless uAPI revision 3 (gus bourg): bit_size is
gone from the uAPI (it was always the payload), so BITS_LEN is the plane
payload. The raw-coding revert and the debug removal have nothing to
revert in the port (see "increase MV buffer size to 112KB").]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c   | 28 ++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
index 23267ab54..7fffd0410 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
@@ -21,13 +21,15 @@
 /* Vendor allocates BPLANE+DCAC+MV as one contiguous block:
  *   BPLANE @ +0x0000  16KB
  *   DCAC   @ +0x4000  16KB
- *   MV     @ +0x8000 112KB
+ *   MV     @ +0x8000 112KB (7 slots x 16KB, rotated per decode)
  * Total = 144KB, 16KB-aligned
  */
 #define VC1_AUX_ALLOC_SIZE		(144 * SZ_1K)
 #define VC1_AUX_BPLANE_OFF		0x0000
 #define VC1_AUX_DCAC_OFF		0x4000
 #define VC1_AUX_MV_OFF			0x8000
+#define MV_SLOT_SIZE			(16 * SZ_1K)
+#define MV_SLOT_COUNT			7
 
 /* Size in bits of the start code which begins an Advanced profile buffer */
 #define VC1_START_CODE_BITS		32
@@ -300,19 +302,19 @@ static int cedrus_vc1_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 		reg |= VE_DEC_VC1_EPHS_EPTB_DET_BYPASS;
 	cedrus_write(dev, VE_DEC_VC1_EPHS, reg);
 
-	/* Set bitstream source */
-
-	buf_size = vb2_plane_size(src_buf, 0);
-	/*
-	 * The vendor decoder keeps the whole multi-frame VBV buffer mapped and
-	 * sets BITS_LEN to the total buffered data, so the bit reader always has
-	 * data ahead of the current frame and the per-frame decode is bounded by
-	 * the macroblock count. The stateless interface hands us a single frame
-	 * per buffer; advertise the whole (page-rounded) source allocation so the
-	 * bitstream DMA does not stall fetching past the frame when the VLD over-
-	 * reads on the last macroblock (STATUS bs_dma_busy -> watchdog timeout).
+	/* Set bitstream source.
+	 *
+	 * The vendor keeps a multi-frame VBV buffer permanently mapped;
+	 * any over-read beyond the current frame lands on valid data of
+	 * the next frame.  The stateless API provides one frame per
+	 * buffer - limit BITS_LEN to the actual frame size so the
+	 * VLD never fetches uninitialized memory past the frame end.
+	 * Keep BITS_END_ADDR at the page-rounded allocation boundary as
+	 * a safety net against runaway DMA (watchdog timeout).
 	 */
-	cedrus_write(dev, VE_DEC_VC1_BITS_LEN, buf_size * 8);
+	buf_size = vb2_plane_size(src_buf, 0);
+	cedrus_write(dev, VE_DEC_VC1_BITS_LEN,
+		     vb2_get_plane_payload(src_buf, 0) * 8);
 	cedrus_write(dev, VE_DEC_VC1_BITS_OFFSET, 0);
 
 	src_buf_addr = vb2_dma_contig_plane_dma_addr(src_buf, 0);
-- 
